{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 -c \\\"\nimport json\nst=json.load(open('state.json'))\ni=[x for x in st['interpretations'] if x['id']=='731fd869048d4d2b85047524f3018c26-interpretation-0'][0]\nr=i['rationale']\nprint(r[:600]); print('...'); print(r[-1500:])\nprint('=== LIM ==='); [print('*',l[:200]) for l in i['limitations']]\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 -c \\\"\nimport json\nst=json.load(open('state.json'))\ni=[x for x in st['interpretations'] if x['id']=='731fd869048d4d2b85047524f3018c26-interpretation-0'][0]\nr=i['rationale']\nprint(r[:600]); print('...'); print(r[-1500:])\nprint('=== LIM ==='); [print('*',l[:200]) for l in i['limitations']]\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"Conclusion: violated, and the scoped defect is asserted. A heartbeat executed on a goroutine other than the main RPC loop, as the fast-path contract permits, races the node's term update: the term it decided to persist can land after a higher term already persisted by the main thread, leaving the node below a term it had adopted. The lower the node's persisted term falls below the current leader's, the more willing it becomes to accept an older leader's messages, and it then replaces an entry it had already applied at the higher term with that leader's entry. Evidence. Consequence, receipt cab\n...\ntbeat request builds (net_transport.go:660-690, replication.go:388-397) - and for that shape calls the registered handler directly on the connection-handler goroutine, skipping the consumer channel (net_transport.go:718-736), with NewRaft registering r.processHeartbeat (api.go:626-632). appendEntries tests a.Term above r.getCurrentTerm(), then calls setCurrentTerm(a.Term), which writes the stable store and afterwards stores the same value atomically without re-checking (raft.go:1470-1490, 2164-2172); the gap between the store write and the atomic store is where a concurrent higher-term writer can be overtaken. The subsequent acceptance and truncation run on the entry path that trusts the current term (raft.go:1526-1566). Consequence under the exercised conditions: a follower whose term write is overtaken by a concurrent heartbeat can finish below an already adopted term and then accept and apply a stale leader's conflicting entries, leaving its log and FSM describing different histories; when that happens the window did not need an artificially delayed store, only the overlap the transport contract permits. The concurrency this depends on is a declared design choice: the target's divergence document states that it performs heartbeating concurrently with other AppendEntries RPCs 'to avoid having to set the election timeout high enough to account for the max acceptable disk operation' (docs/divergence.md:25-34), so the term update must remain correct under exactly this overlap.\n=== LIM ===\n* Two timing modes, 200 attempts each, run three times on one platform: the jittered case produced 90, 97 and then 105 inversions, and the no-delay case produced 0, 0 and then 2. These counts are proper\n* The two competing leaders were modelled by crafted requests over the real consumer path; the obsolete leader's partition, its continued heartbeating and the newer leader's quorum were not produced by \n* Only the term and leader writes of the fast-path were exercised; whether other concurrent fast-path effects interact with snapshot installation or configuration updates was not tested.\n* The jitter distribution is a uniform 0-2 ms added to every current-term write; no case swept the delay magnitude, so how the rate scales with store latency is not measured.\n* The fix boundary is unexamined: a compare-and-set term update would close this interleaving, but no protective mechanism in the captured code was tested against it.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
